cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Almaty Springs: A Geospatial and Hydrochemical Study of Natural Springs
  in the Almaty Region
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, its code, or the laboratory results derived from it,
  please cite the project and credit all authors listed below.
type: dataset

# Contributions are described in README.md, section 11. CFF 1.2.0 has no field
# for author roles, so they are not duplicated here.
authors:
  - family-names: Karelin
    given-names: Vladislav
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2612-7843
    alias: x1n0x
    city: Almaty
    country: KZ
  - family-names: Katkova
    given-names: Elizaveta
    affiliation: Kazakh-German University (DKU), Almaty
    city: Almaty
    country: KZ
    # ORCID pending. Transliteration of Cyrillic surnames varies between
    # databases, so an identifier matters more here than for a Latin-script
    # name -- add it as soon as there is one.

abstract: >-
  An open inventory and hydrochemical study of natural springs on the northern
  slope of the Ile-Alatau range and within the Almaty urban area. The project
  combines OpenStreetMap-derived locations, DEM elevation, geotagged field
  photographs, and laboratory water analysis to describe where springs occur
  and how their water chemistry varies. Laboratory work is carried out at the
  Kazakh-German University (DKU) in Almaty.

keywords:
  - hydrology
  - springs
  - water quality
  - hydrochemistry
  - geospatial
  - OpenStreetMap
  - Almaty
  - Kazakhstan
  - open data

repository-code: https://github.com/x1n0x/almaty-springs
url: https://x1n0x.github.io/almaty-springs/
license: MIT
